Aetna Commercial Coverage Policy: Neuroimaging for Headache.
Routine imaging for primary headache disorders is not covered.
EXCEPTIONS — coverage applies for new headache when ANY of:
(a) Thunderclap onset (worst-headache-of-life with sudden onset);
(b) New focal neurologic deficit;
(c) Onset after age 50 with new pattern;
(d) Immunocompromised host;
(e) History of malignancy;
(f) Trauma within prior 30 days;
(g) Meningismus or papilledema on exam.
Negative non-contrast CT does NOT rule out subarachnoid hemorrhage or vascular abnormality beyond 6 hours post-onset; MRI/MRA is the appropriate next study when thunderclap presentation persists.

Cigna Specialty Drug Policy: Natalizumab (J2350) for MS.
Natalizumab is a second-line therapy. Coverage requires:
(1) Documented relapsing-remitting MS;
(2) JCV antibody status known (negative or low-positive <0.9);
(3) Failed or intolerant of at least ONE first-line disease-modifying therapy (interferon beta, glatiramer acetate, dimethyl fumarate, teriflunomide, or fingolimod) with EITHER documented intolerance OR breakthrough disease activity (clinical relapse or new MRI lesion);
(4) Provider attestation of PML risk discussion.
